cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "raman-open-ml: trustworthy, reproducible machine learning for Raman spectroscopy"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "raman-open-ml contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/JoulesSpace/raman-ml"
abstract: >
  An open-source toolkit for Raman spectroscopy machine learning on public,
  openly-licensed data. It covers classification and concentration
  quantification and adds the trustworthy-ML layer the field keeps flagging as
  open: uncertainty quantification (conformal prediction, temperature scaling,
  deep ensembles), open-set / out-of-distribution rejection, calibration
  transfer across instruments, and domain-shift-aware evaluation.
keywords:
  - Raman spectroscopy
  - machine learning
  - chemometrics
  - conformal prediction
  - out-of-distribution detection
  - calibration transfer
  - domain shift
license: AGPL-3.0-or-later
version: 0.1.0
